reflection
In 150-250 words: What did AI notice that you missed? What did AI invent or overreach on? Which requirement changed after review? Why must requirements have evidence?

What AI caught that I had missed: 
The ai caught the FR-03 FR-05 date field contradtioction, the story 3 gp only visibility with no authentication model behind it, the AI also notied FR-02's blank search rejection was described in story 2 but never written into the FR itself. these were real gaps I had overlooked while writing the FRs. 

What AI invented or overreached on: 
it raised patient  double booking across two GPs as a problem. but that was never mentioned by the client. I assume the AI comapared this system to other scheduling systems rather than working with the evidence provided. I rejected this as a requirement, although I will keep it as a possible question to ask the client in the future. 

which requirment changed after review: 
NFR-04 had the most change. it originally had no pass fail condition due to the wording. I reworded it around a messurable control diff test. 

Why requirements need evidence: 
without any evidence, it's easy to accept AI suggestions that sound reasonable but arn't supported by client brief. tagging each suggestion as accepted, modifed, rejected or unverifed kept the decision traceable and allowed me to see the difference between AI assumptions and real client requiests. 







